+The pair-gap derivation defines A(0)=<e_0,(-K^2)^-1 e_0> and D(0)=1/(6h^2). Its normalized signed two-neighbor vector u has <u,(-K^2)^-1u>=A(0) for perpendicular pairs and D(0) for opposite pairs. Since ||b_A||=sqrt(2)h,
