+The auxiliary trace is over its full Fock space at chemical potential zero, not a fixed-number thermal trace. The full physical thermal partition function still sums over all native sectors. A maximal individual sector weight does not establish concentration. At $t=0$ all sectors tie and the full Hamiltonian vanishes; no nonzero-hopping theorem is required.
